  "preamble": "Vocalization of the labio-velar approximant [w] into the high back rounded vowel [u]. It typically happens when [w] loses its syllable margin, as when Old English final -w after a consonant became -u (Proto-Germanic *balwą > bealu 'harm, evil').",
